I wrote the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md but did not commit it. session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit command you gave does nothing. I force-added it and committed once, then undid that local commit to keep an ignored file out of the repo. The file is on disk for the planner, and HEAD is back at 91d5a862.

What the assessment says:
• Build is green. CI passed on the latest commits, and the last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks with no reverts. A one-shot yoyo -p prompt worked (exit 0), with one small nuisance: a stray "watch: no files changed" line at the end of piped output.
• #1065 is real; I reproduced it. In a scratch repo with a file git clean can't delete, yoyo undo --all prints ✗ failed to clean untracked files and then ✓ reverted all uncommitted changes, exiting 1.
• The model is misinformed too. Reading the code (not run in the REPL), in that same failure the model is told deleted locked/f (was untracked) for a file that still exists, and the undo history is cleared anyway. src/commands_git.rs is exactly at its size ceiling of 3753 lines, so new tests belong in src/commands_git_undo_tests.rs.
• The 401 hint ignores keys passed by flag (#1062). It decides whether a key exists by checking only the environment variable (src/prompt_retry.rs:524). A user who passed --api-key is told the key "is not set" and advised to use --api-key. The first-run setup wizard has the same blind spot.
• Codex and Claude Code just fixed #1063's problem in their own tools. Codex 0.163.0 and Claude Code 2.1.305 both shipped fixes for waiting on a background child that holds the output pipe open, which is what #1063 asks for in /bg and /watch. yoyo's /run fix from this morning is the in-tree reference.
• Possible mislabel after sub-agent fallback (read, not run). Claude Code 2.1.305 fixed naming the wrong model after a sub-agent switches to its fallback. yoyo's error report says which of the two models failed "is not observable here", but the component that does the switching holds that information. This needs a probe before it becomes a task.
• I saved the competitor findings to yopedia (queued). Recall only gave me note titles, because the question endpoint answered "Sign in required".

Ranked for the planner:
1. #1065.
2. #1062 (both places).
3. #1063, starting with a probe that runs the bug.
4. Extend the opt-in key scrub to the other places yoyo starts processes, without changing its default.

